Z||000003||artherd||12-06-2001||09:02 PM||||Yep! count 'em  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Actually, the more splines you have, typically the shallower they are. (and deeper for fewer, etc)<P>I'm not really sure which is better, though either extreme isn't good (120 splines would be too many, 2 would be too few  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Yeah, it's not a horribly big input shaft... and our trannys don't even use Pilot bearings!  Zoikes man!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Turbo88:<BR><B>there are only 14 splines on that shaft? wow...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
